  "body": "The chamfer/taper kind is a sharp cone only: no tip diameter, no tip radius, and no tapered flank above a non-sharp tip.\n\n**Where:** `Taper` is \"a cone widening upward from its virtual sharp tip\" (`crates/tools/src/tools.rs`, Taper doc; `is_sane` near `:305`).\n\n**Effect:**\n- Flat-tip chamfer mills, V-engravers with a point radius, countersinks and combined center drills (both with a real tip diameter), and tapered end mills with a ball or flat tip can't be described.\n- Writing them as sharp cones misstates where the cutter actually is: the depth for a given chamfer width is wrong by the tip.\n\n**Fix sketch:** `Taper` gains an optional tip diameter and tip radius (and a tip form: flat or ball). The chamfer-depth math, the sim and the gouge laws use the real tip.\n\nEffort: max (geometry).\n\n**Done means:** a flat-tip chamfer and a radiused-point V-bit chamfer to the right width at the right depth; pinned.\n",
